Condition : 57 - Before the purpose built student accommodation hereby permitted is first occupied or brought into use, a full Student Accommodation Management Plan must be  submitted to the Local Planning Authority and approved in writing. The management plan must include:  

 

Management procedures along with details of the day-to-day operations of the Development; 

Methodologies to manage student vehicle movements comprising arrivals and departures at the start and end of semesters; 

The locations and layouts of the Kitchenette/cooking facilities to ensure sufficient space for food preparation; 

Arrangements for fast food deliveries  

Measures to prevent congestion and obstruction to the local highway network and to preserve the amenity of local residents.  

Provision of a welcome pack to each Occupant explaining the management arrangements 

 

Reason: In order to protect the amenity of the wider area and the living conditions of future occupiers.
